@startuml LogiShop_UseCase_Simplified
!theme plain
' Compact thesis figure — fewer ovals & arrows (similar spirit to short tourism DSS diagram)
scale 0.82
skinparam dpi 110
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam titleFontSize 13
skinparam ArrowThickness 0.8
skinparam actorStyle stick
skinparam usecase {
  BackgroundColor #FFFACD
  BorderColor #333333
  FontSize 9
}
skinparam actor {
  FontSize 9
}
skinparam RectangleBorderStyle dashed
skinparam RectangleBackgroundColor #FFFEEE

title Figure 3.x. Use case diagram — LogiShop\n(Logistics visibility & routing DSS)

left to right direction

'--- Same inheritance idea as tourism DSS: Guest ← Registered user ← Administrator ---
actor "Guest" as G
actor "Registered user\n(Customer)" as R
actor "Administrator" as A

G <|-- R
R <|-- A

rectangle "LogiShop\n(Logistics visibility & routing DSS)" {

  usecase "Log in" as UC_LOG
  usecase "Browse public content\n(home & locations catalog)" as UC_BRW

  usecase "Submit shipment request" as UC_SUB
  usecase "View and track\nmy orders" as UC_MINE

  usecase "View all orders\n(staff scope)" as UC_ALL
  usecase "Manage platform data\n& approvals" as UC_OPS

  usecase "Verify credentials" as UC_VRF
  usecase "Complete shipment form" as UC_FRM
  usecase "View route on\noperations map" as UC_MAP
}

'--- Context note **outside** system boundary (UML: linked with dashed line)
note as ContextDoc #FFF9B2
  **Context — problem & environment**
  Decision support for **international shipment** handling:
  * Orders are reviewed before customers see full details (approval gate).
  * **Track visibility** uses carrier scan data (e.g. UPS) for status and map paths.
  * **Route / operations map** supports spatial awareness and re-planning views.
  * Staff maintain **reference data** (locations catalog, FX rates for quoted amounts).
  **Scope:** Web prototype; human remains accountable for final operational decisions.

  ----
  **Typical activities under “Manage platform data & approvals”**
  Review queue · Approve / reject · Correct shipment data · Assign tracking ·
  Staff notes & delivery status · User directory & statistics
end note

UC_OPS .. ContextDoc

UC_LOG ..> UC_VRF : <<include>>
UC_SUB ..> UC_FRM : <<include>>
UC_MINE <.. UC_MAP : <<extend>>

'--- Guest
G --> UC_LOG
G --> UC_BRW

'--- Registered user (Customer)
R --> UC_LOG
R --> UC_BRW
R --> UC_SUB
R --> UC_MINE

'--- Administrator (inherits customer capabilities in this model + staff duties)
A --> UC_LOG
A --> UC_BRW
A --> UC_SUB
A --> UC_MINE
A --> UC_ALL
A --> UC_OPS

@enduml
